
# Scratch directory used for one-off manual probes.
.probe/

# Next 16 regenerates this on every dev/build run, and writes a *different* import
# per mode: `next build` wants .next/types/routes.d.ts, `next dev` wants
# .next/dev/types/routes.d.ts. A tracked copy is therefore dirty in one mode or the
# other, forever, and committing the build-mode version breaks typecheck in a fresh
# checkout where .next does not exist yet. next dev, next build and next typegen all
# create it before anything needs it, and tsconfig lists it in include, so its
# absence is harmless.
next-env.d.ts
